@startuml evidence_dataflow
' Static evidence extraction data flow - drawn only from evidence/extract.py (main)
' and docs/contracts/resource-evidence.md. Built behaviour only; nothing planned is shown.
' Owner: M1 (Zoya Ahmad). Slot: ch5:fig:evidence-dfd.
skinparam dpi 200
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F7F7F7
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #333333
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFFEE
title analyse_pair(project, polluter, victim, depth=2, deepen=True)\nevidence/extract.py

start
:inputs: compiled class folders
(target/classes, target/test-classes; read only),
polluter and victim as Class#method,
depth 1..5 (default 2);
:used = depth;
repeat
  partition "analyse_test(project, test, used)\nfor the polluter, then the victim" {
    :find_roots: the test class and its project superclasses;
    note right
      roots: the test method,
      @Before / @After, @BeforeClass / @AfterClass,
      JUnit 3 setUp / tearDown,
      the test class's <clinit>;
      overridden methods are skipped
    end note
    :walk_root: breadth-first from each root,
    each method at most once per root;
    :Project.load(class): javap -v -p -c,
    parsed into ClassInfo, Method and
    Instruction objects, cached per class;
    :scan_method / scan_call: one bytecode instruction at a time
    * getstatic / putstatic -> static-field READ / WRITE
    * System.getProperty / setProperty / clearProperty,
       Integer.getInteger, Long.getLong, Boolean.getBoolean
       with a constant key -> system-property READ / WRITE
    * call into a project class -> follow_call queues the
       named target one level deeper (DEPTH_LIMIT if too deep)
    * call into the JDK or a library -> external_calls_not_followed
    * anything else it cannot model -> typed unsupported observation;
    note right
      unsupported kinds:
      REFLECTION, INVOKEDYNAMIC,
      VIRTUAL_DISPATCH, UNRESOLVED_CALL,
      SYSPROP_NON_CONSTANT_KEY, SYSPROP_BULK,
      IMPLICIT_CLINIT, DEPTH_LIMIT,
      JUNIT_RULE_OR_RUNNER
    end note
    :Output 1 per test:
    accesses (resource, READ / WRITE, class, method,
    bytecode_offset, via, depth, call_path),
    unsupported_observations,
    external_calls_not_followed;
  }
  :find_edges: resources the polluter WRITES that the victim READS;
  :Output 2: edges with every write
  and read location,
  no_supported_resource_evidence = no edges,
  both tests' observations,
  the 7 fixed limitations;
repeat while (no edge, deepen on,\na DEPTH_LIMIT hit, used < 5?) is (yes: used + 1)
->no;
:record depth_requested and depth_used;
:report_fields(pair):
first edge -> shared_resource,
its first write -> polluter_write_location,
its first read -> victim_read_location,
limitations (+ other edges and locations,
evidence deeper than depth 2);
note right
  used by runner/cli.py: analyse_pair once
  per polluter, combined by combine_fields,
  then put in the report by eval/report.py.
  The command line prints Output 1 / 2 as JSON.
end note
stop
@enduml
